//! Byte signatures for the radio-bypass targets.
//!
//! Generated by `cargo run -p flashimg --example derive-signature`. The masks
//! are not stored: [`Signature::from_xtensa`] recomputes them from the code,
//! so the rule and the data cannot drift apart.
//!
//! # Why there is more than one of each
//!
//! A function's compiled form belongs to a *compilation*, not to a project.
//! `esp_phy_enable` is ESP-IDF's own code, so any project built against the
//! same IDF with the same options produces the same bytes -- which is what
//! makes a signature portable across firmware from different authors, and the
//! whole reason this works on an image we have never seen.
//!
//! Change the IDF version, the chip, or an sdkconfig option that reaches this
//! code, and it is a different function. `esp_phy_enable` is 138 bytes in one
//! ESP32-S3 configuration, 154 in another, and 150 on plain ESP32.
//!
//! So the table holds variants, each tagged with where it came from, and
//! matching tries all of them. Supporting a new IDF is data, not code: derive
//! from any build of it that ships a `.elf` and paste the result in.
//!
//! # Known gaps
//!
//! - `esp_wifi_connect` and `esp_wifi_disconnect` are absent from every
//!   variant. Both compile to ten bytes -- a stack frame, one call, a return
//!   -- which matched six places in a single image. A signature that cannot
//!   tell its function from five others is not a signature.
//! - **IDF v5.4 is not covered.** Arduino-built firmware uses it and none of
//!   the builds available here do, so there was nothing to derive from. Such
//!   an image finds some targets and misses others, and the miss is reported
//!   rather than skipped silently.

use crate::signature::Signature;

/// One function as compiled in one build.
#[derive(Debug)]
pub struct Variant {
    pub symbol: &'static str,
    /// Which compilation these bytes came from, so a match can say what it
    /// recognised rather than just asserting it found something.
    pub source: &'static str,
    code: &'static [u8],
}

